/ Build one .goal file: decide which actions each step uses, let the LLM write each step's actions in
/ formal, read them into the steps, then recurse into sub-goals.
Start

/ A cached goal — the source its .pr was built from, every step and sub-goal cached — isn't built:
/ its cache stands.
- if %goal.IsCached%, return %goal.Cache%
- call /system/builder/EmitBuildEvent kind="goalHeader", goal=%goal%
- set %buildStart% = %Now.Ticks%
- set %trace% = {"id": "%!trace.id%", "timestamp": "%Now%", "goal": "%goal.Name%", "subGoals": [], "durationMs": 0}
- call Compile, on error call HandleBuildFailure

- set %parentGoal% = %goal%
- foreach %parentGoal.Child%, call BuildSubGoal subGoal=%item%
- set %goal% = %parentGoal%

- math.subtract A=%Now.Ticks%, B=%buildStart%, write to %elapsedTicks%
- math.divide A=%elapsedTicks%, B=10000, write to %elapsedMs%
- set %trace.durationMs% = %elapsedMs%

- save %trace% to file '/.build/traces/%!trace.id%/%goal.Name%.json'
- add %goal.Name% to %traceGoals%
/ Re-parent indented sub-steps into the preceding condition's gate-action Child (recurses sub-goals). Post-compile, pre-save.
- build.fold Goal=%goal%, on error call HandleBuildFailure
- build.goalsSave Goal=%goal%


/ The three stages for the goal in %goal% — shared by the top goal and every sub-goal. The decider
/ answers WHICH actions a step may use; the LLM writes each step's actions in formal; the steps read
/ the answer, each checking its own line, and take their code. A step refused goes back to the LLM
/ alone; an else written apart from its if is the programmer's to fix, not the LLM's.
Compile
/ Steps that are all cached have nothing to ask.
- if %goal.Step.IsCached%, return
/ Steps each cached or written in formal need no answer: the formal ones read their own text.
- condition.if(Left=%goal.Step.IsAnswered%) { build.match(Goal=%goal%, Answer=""); goal.return() }
- call Decide
- call Properties
- build.match(Goal=%goal%, Answer=%answer%); on.error(Key="UnwrittenNumber", Recovery=[goal.call(Name="ConfirmNumbers")]); on.error(Key="ElseWithoutIf", Recovery=[goal.call(Name="SourceError")]); on.error(Recovery=[goal.call(Name="FixSteps")])


/ The answer was refused for some steps — each refusal names its step and every problem at once.
/ Continue the conversation with them; only those steps are answered again, and the others keep the
/ code they took. The answer is read again here, so numbers it leaves to confirm are confirmed too.
FixSteps
- call /system/builder/EmitBuildEvent kind="properties-rejected", errorMessage=%!error.Message%
- set %fixMessages% = [{"Role":"user", "Content":"Steps %!error.Details.steps% were refused: %!error.Message%. Answer again only these steps, one line each, starting with its [i], in formal."}]
- llm.query Message=%fixMessages%, Model="gpt-5.4-nano", cache=%!build.setting.cache%, continuePreviousConversation=true, write to %answer%
- build.match(Goal=%goal%, Answer=%answer%); on.error(Key="UnwrittenNumber", Recovery=[goal.call(Name="ConfirmNumbers")])


/ The answer's code writes numbers its steps don't write as digits ("retry once" → 1). Whether the words
/ give them is the decider's to say, one yes/no per number; the answer is read again with those answers,
/ and a number the decider denies is refused as invented.
ConfirmNumbers
- set %numbers% = %!error.Details.numbers%
- render template "/system/builder/llm/templates/confirm.state.template", write to %confirmState%
- render template "/system/builder/llm/templates/confirm.template", write to %confirmQuestions%
- llm.decider State=%confirmState%, Question=%confirmQuestions%, write to %confirmed%
- build.match Goal=%goal%, Answer=%answer%, Confirmed=%confirmed%


/ Sub-goal recursion — the same three stages, attached to the parent trace.
BuildSubGoal
- set %goal% = %subGoal%
- call /system/builder/EmitBuildEvent kind="subGoalHeader", goal=%goal%
- set %subgoalStart% = %Now.Ticks%
- call Compile, on error call HandleBuildFailure
- add {goal: "%goal.Name%"} to %trace.subGoals%
- math.subtract A=%Now.Ticks%, B=%subgoalStart%, write to %elapsedTicks%
- math.divide A=%elapsedTicks%, B=10000, write to %subgoalMs%
- call /system/builder/EmitBuildEvent kind="subGoalDone", goal=%goal%, subgoalMs=%subgoalMs%


/ The programmer's plang is wrong, not the LLM's answer, so nothing is retried. The LLM writes the
/ corrected plang for the programmer; the same error is raised again carrying it, and the build of
/ this goal stops there.
SourceError
- render template "/system/builder/llm/SourceFix.llm", write to %sourceFixSystem%
- set %sourceFixMessages% = [{"Role":"system", "Content":"%sourceFixSystem%"}, {"Role":"user", "Content":"%!error.Key%: %!error.Message%\n\nThe goal:\n%goal%"}]
- llm.query Message=%sourceFixMessages%, Model="gpt-5.4-nano", cache=%!build.setting.cache%, write to %sourceFix%
- throw %!error%, fix suggestion %sourceFix%


/ Capture error onto trace, save, rethrow. No null-pass inference.
HandleBuildFailure
- call /system/builder/EmitBuildEvent kind="goalError", goal=%goal%, errorMessage=%!error.Message%, fix=%!error.FixSuggestion%
- set %trace.buildError% = {"key": "%!error.Key%", "message": "%!error.Message%", "goal": "%goal.Name%"}
- save %trace% to file '/.build/traces/%!trace.id%/%goal.Name%.json'
- throw %!error%
